# Local development against Floci (local AWS). Every value here is a non-secret dev default.
AWS_ENDPOINT_URL=http://localhost:4567
AWS_ENDPOINT_URL_S3=http://localhost:4567
AWS_S3_FORCE_PATH_STYLE=true
AWS_REGION=us-east-1
AWS_DEFAULT_REGION=us-east-1
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=test
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=test
RIDECORE_TABLE=ridecore
RIDECORE_JWT_SECRET=dev-only-not-a-secret-for-local-and-ci
# Precedence everywhere (scripts/load-env.ts): exported env > .env.local > .env.deploy > this file.
# .env.local (git-ignored) is yours, e.g. a custom RIDECORE_JWT_SECRET; nothing generated writes it.
# `make up` writes .env.deploy (git-ignored) with RIDECORE_TABLE from the CDK output and
# RIDECORE_API_URL for the Floci-deployed API; `npm run dev` serves the same API on port 3000.
# ridecore-location (Go service, optional). Unset = dispatch reads the DynamoDB index as always.
# `make up LOCATION=1` writes these to .env.local if absent. The key is the service's dev-only internal
# key (its .env.example); Lambdas on Floci use the *_LAMBDA_URL, local processes the plain URL.
# RIDECORE_LOCATION_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8090
# RIDECORE_LOCATION_LAMBDA_URL=http://host.docker.internal:8090
# RIDECORE_LOCATION_WS_URL=ws://127.0.0.1:8090
# RIDECORE_LOCATION_KEY=dev-only-location-internal-key-change-me
